@startuml upload-lifecycle
' One notification, from webhook to Strava activity.
'
' The question this diagram exists to answer: where does the flow retry, where
' does it stop, and where does it deliberately do nothing? Getting those three
' apart is what keeps the DLQ free of messages no retry could ever fix.
'
' Rendered by `make diagrams` (phase 8). Do not hand-edit the SVG.

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 12

participant "Google\nHealth" as GH
participant "receiver\n(Function URL)" as RX
queue "SQS\n(+DLQ)" as Q
participant "worker" as W
database "DynamoDB" as DB
participant "Strava" as ST

== notification ==

GH -> RX : POST /  (Authorization: <secret>)
note right of RX
  hmac.compare_digest on the header.
  The ECDSA signature is *not* checked —
  stdlib cannot, and the receiver trusts
  nothing in the body. See PLAN.md §8.
end note
RX -> Q : {"type":"notification", body}
RX --> GH : **204**
note left of GH
  204 specifically. Anything else is a
  failed delivery: retried with backoff
  for 7 days, then discarded.
end note

== fetch and correct ==

Q -> W : notification
W -> DB : read TOKEN#google
W -> GH : GET .../exercise/dataPoints  (no filter)
note right of W
  The notification carries the interval,
  so no day-wide listing and no diffing.
  Dedupe is still required: at-least-once.

  The window is applied *client-side*: the
  API rejects every documented spelling of
  its filter for the exercise data type.
  The listing is newest-first, so paging
  stops as soon as it passes the window.
  See PLAN.md §8.
end note

loop each exercise in the window
  W -> DB : read LOG#{exerciseId}
  alt already processed
    W -> W : drop, silently
  else new
    W -> GH : GET ...:exportExerciseTcx?alt=media&partialData=true
    W -> W : rescale_tcx(bytes)
    note right of W
      Pure, offline, no network.
      Three outcomes, and only one
      of them means "do not upload".
    end note

    alt corrected
      W -> ST : POST /uploads  (external_id = exerciseId)
    else uncorrectable — yoga, no GPS, partial GPS
      W -> ST : POST /uploads  (unchanged bytes)
      note right of W
        **Pass through, never drop.**
        Correcting is not a precondition
        for reaching Strava.
      end note
    else withheld
      W -> DB : write LOG#{id} = withheld(reason)
      note right of W : deterministic; never retried
    end
    W -> Q : {"type":"upload_check", attempt:1} (DelaySeconds 20)
  end
end

== the upload is asynchronous ==

Q -> W : upload_check
W -> ST : GET /uploads/{id}
alt activity_id set
  W -> DB : write LOG#{id} = uploaded(activity_id)
else error names a duplicate
  W -> DB : write LOG#{id} = uploaded(duplicate)
  note right of W
    Strava dedupes on external_id.
    A redelivered webhook costs one
    rejected upload, not a second
    activity in someone's feed.
  end note
else error otherwise
  W -> DB : write LOG#{id} = failed(error)
  note right of W : deterministic; do not re-upload
else still processing
  alt attempt < 5
    W -> Q : upload_check, attempt+1 (DelaySeconds 20, 40, 80...)
    note right of W
      Re-enqueue, never sleep. A sleeping
      Lambda is billed wall-clock time.
    end note
  else attempt == 5
    W -> DB : write LOG#{id} = failed(timeout)
    note right of W
      Stop. A slow Strava is not a
      poisoned message, and does not
      belong in the DLQ.
    end note
  end
end

== what is allowed to reach the DLQ ==

note across
  Only **transient** faults propagate: NetworkError, RateLimited, ServerError —
  everything carrying the `Transient` marker. `http.retrying` has already tried
  them four times with backoff, honouring Retry-After. Everything else is a
  decision written to DynamoDB and never seen again.
end note

@enduml
